  "sentences": [
    {"text": "Russet and amber leaves spiralled to the ground, one by one, as if the trees were counting.", "vibe": "Beautiful"},
    {"text": "Burnished, copper beeches flamed against the grey sky.", "vibe": "Beautiful"},
    {"text": "Crisp, brittle leaves crunched underfoot all the way to school.", "vibe": "General"},
    {"text": "Mellow, golden sunlight slanted through the orchard and lit each apple like a lamp.", "vibe": "Peaceful"},
    {"text": "Thin, blue bonfire smoke drifted across the gardens.", "vibe": "General"},
    {"text": "Delicate, dew-beaded cobwebs glittered in the hedges.", "vibe": "Beautiful"},
    {"text": "Plump, glossy conkers thudded onto the path and split their spiny cases.", "vibe": "Lively"},
    {"text": "A wild, blustery gale stripped the branches bare in a single night.", "vibe": "Wild"},
    {"text": "Bare, skeletal branches clawed at the sky.", "vibe": "Lonely"},
    {"text": "A thick, sodden carpet of leaves rotted in the gutters.", "vibe": "General"},
    {"text": "On cool, misty mornings, a white ribbon of vapour hung over the river.", "vibe": "Peaceful"},
    {"text": "Busy, bright-eyed squirrels hoarded acorns as though time were running out.", "vibe": "Lively"},
    {"text": "Long, ragged skeins of geese honked overhead, heading south.", "vibe": "Lonely"},
    {"text": "Ripe, windfall apples lay scattered in the grass, humming with wasps.", "vibe": "General"},
    {"text": "A damp, earthy smell of decay rose from the ground beneath the trees.", "vibe": "Menacing"},
    {"text": "The short, grey afternoons faded by four o'clock, and the lamps were lit at tea time.", "vibe": "Lonely"},
    {"text": "Leaves whirled across the playground, and the children chased them.", "vibe": "Lively"},
    {"text": "A heap of garden rubbish smouldered at the bottom of the garden for days.", "vibe": "General"},
    {"text": "The wind roared through the wood and sent the leaves up in great, wheeling flocks.", "vibe": "Wild"},
    {"text": "Rain and gale together flattened the last of the dahlias.", "vibe": "Wild"},
    {"text": "The swallows thinned along the wires and then, one morning, were gone.", "vibe": "Lonely"},
    {"text": "There was a melancholy sweetness in the air, the smell of things ending.", "vibe": "Lonely"},
    {"text": "Pale fungi sprouted overnight from the rotting stump.", "vibe": "Menacing"},
    {"text": "Fog and dusk arrived together, and the lane filled with the smell of wet leaves.", "vibe": "Menacing"},
    {"text": "The whole hillside glowed crimson and gold, as though it had been set alight.", "vibe": "Beautiful"},
    {"text": "Frost edged every fallen leaf with silver.", "vibe": "Beautiful"},
    {"text": "Berries ripened in the hedgerows, and the stubble fields lay quiet in the sun.", "vibe": "Peaceful"},
    {"text": "It was the kind of still, bright day when sound carries for miles.", "vibe": "Peaceful"},
    {"text": "They gathered the harvest before the weather turned.", "vibe": "General"},
    {"text": "Sparks flew up from the bonfire, and faces shone in the firelight.", "vibe": "Lively"}
  ]
